Body:
I think that this may be that the `Foundry Base Models` use a different endpoint from the standard models. I got my `Kimi-K2.5` to respond to the text (with quota exceeded I must admit) with setting the endpoint manually.
Here is the respective part of my config:
```json
    "provider": {
        "azure-foundry-base-models": {
            "name": "Azure Foundry Base Models",
            "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
            "options": {
                "baseURL": "https://swedencentral.api.cognitive.microsoft.com/openai/v1"
            },
            "models": {
                "Kimi-K2.5": {
                    "name": "Kimi-K2.5"
                }
            }
        }
    },
```
You can find the endpoint on the page of the model deployment in the code example.

I cannot say however, why I have the quota exceeded issue, since I when using curl I get the answer just fine:
```sh
$  curl -s "https://swedencentral.api.cognitive.microsoft.com/openai/v1/chat/completions" \                                                                                                                                                                           
         -H "Authorization: Bearer $AZURE_API_KEY" \
         -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
         -d '{"model": "Kimi-K2.5", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Tell me hi!"}]}'
